# Global Policy Evolution

- Read the `global-policy-evolution` skill before changing project policy.
- Scope: open **git repository root** only — never `~/.cursor`, `~/.claude`,
  `~/.codex`, or `~/.agents` as project policy.
- Canonical: `AGENTS.md` + `.cursor/` (rules, skills, agents, hooks).
- Mirrors (self-manage via sync): `.claude/`, `.github/copilot-instructions.md`,
  `.github/instructions/`, `.agents/skills/`, managed `CLAUDE.md`.
- After canonical edits: run `sync_policy.py` then full `validate_policy.py`.
- Reject secrets, unsafe links or symlinks, and speculative guidance. Replace
  contradicted policy rather than preserving dual paths.
- Optional `.cursor/policy-config.json`: `forbiddenPolicyNames`, `enabledHosts`,
  `syncEnabled`. MCP stays user-level editor config.

## Policy asset naming

Every rule, skill, agent, and hook basename uses exactly one ownership prefix.

**In this marketplace repo**, the prefix **must match the plugin directory**
that owns the asset (see root `AGENTS.md`):

| Prefix | Plugin |
|---|---|
| `global-*` | `plugins/global/` |
| `code-*` | `plugins/code/` |
| `business-analyst-*` (or exact `business-analyst`) | `plugins/business-analyst/` |
| `agentmemory-*` (or exact `agentmemory`) | `plugins/agentmemory/` |
| `atlassian-*` (or exact `atlassian`) | `plugins/atlassian/` |
| `github-*` (or exact `github`) | `plugins/github/` |
| `jenkins-*` (or exact `jenkins`) | `plugins/jenkins/` |
| `browser-*` | `plugins/browser/` |
| `drawio-*` | `plugins/drawio/` |
| `lucidchart-*` | `plugins/lucidchart/` |
| `google-workspace-*` (or exact `google-workspace`) | `plugins/google-workspace/` |
| `google-cloud-*` (or exact `google-cloud`) | `plugins/google-cloud/` |
| `freshservice-*` (or exact `freshservice`) | `plugins/freshservice/` |
| `vault-*` (or exact `vault`) | `plugins/vault/` |
| `grafana-*` (or exact `grafana`) | `plugins/grafana/` |
| `cloudflare-*` (or exact `cloudflare`) | `plugins/cloudflare/` |
| `compose-*` (or exact `compose`) | `plugins/compose/` |
| `kubernetes-*` (or exact `kubernetes`) | `plugins/kubernetes/` |
| `proxmox-*` (or exact `proxmox`) | `plugins/proxmox/` |
| `argocd-*` (or exact `argocd`) | `plugins/argocd/` |
| `prometheus-*` (or exact `prometheus`) | `plugins/prometheus/` |
| `graylog-*` (or exact `graylog`) | `plugins/graylog/` |
| `minio-*` (or exact `minio`) | `plugins/minio/` |
| `velero-*` (or exact `velero`) | `plugins/velero/` |
| `fortigate-*` (or exact `fortigate`) | `plugins/fortigate/` |
| `yarr-*` (or exact `yarr`) | `plugins/yarr/` |

When promoting policy **into a consuming project** (not this marketplace), use:

| Prefix | Use for |
|---|---|
| `global-*` | Portable craft copied from the `global` plugin |
| `code-*` | Coding standards / workflow copied from the `code` plugin |
| `<project>-*` | Repo-specific contracts, runtimes, and workflow hooks |
| `<component>-*` | Guidance owned by one component or package |

Prefer path globs over `alwaysApply: true` whenever the guidance only matters
for matching paths. Keep `alwaysApply: true` only for session-wide posture
(for example `global-execute-first`, MCP-first, host-url). AgentMemory
capture/recall may stay always-on **with an availability gate** (skip when
the MCP is not connected). Tracker rules stay **agent-requested**
(`alwaysApply: false`) so cold clones without a tracker do not load them
every turn.
